From: Jacob Cook <jacobmcook1984@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: rg35xx-2024: Keep the second SD card powered

The second SD slot's supply (vcc3v3-mmc2, PE4) is switched off when the
card is powered down for system suspend, but the slot's pins stay
pulled up from the always-on vcc-io rail, so the card is back-powered
through its I/O lines for the whole sleep and can come up busy.

Keep the supply on, as Anbernic's firmware effectively does: its device
tree names PE4 "pwr-gpios", which the vendor driver never reads, so the
card is never switched off there. The boot slot is powered from vcc-io
directly and does not show the problem.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024.dts
@@ -334,6 +334,8 @@
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		regulator-name = "vcc3v3-mmc2";
+		/* The card is back-powered through its pulled-up I/O pins when this is off. */
+		regulator-always-on;
 	};
 
 	reg_usb0_vbus: regulator-usb0-vbus {
